1. Understand the Problem: Miguel uses 2 pads of paper each week. Each pad has 30 sheets of paper. We want to find out how many sheets of paper he uses every month. 2. Find the number of sheets per week: Since Miguel uses 2 pads of paper per week and each pad has 30 sheets, the number of sheets he uses per week is 2 pads * 30 sheets/pad = 60 sheets/week. 3. Find the number of sheets per month: There are approximately 4 weeks in a month. Therefore, the number of sheets he uses per month is 60 sheets/week * 4 weeks/month = 240 sheets/month. 4. Final Answer: 240
So the answer is 240.
\boxed{240}
